blueprint:
  name: Philips Hue Remote
  author: mmagin
  domain: automation
  homeassistant:
    min_version: 2024.10.0
  input:
    version_info:
      name: Version History
      description: |-
        - **2026.08.2: Retarget from the Tap Dial (RDM002) to the Dimmer Switch (RWL022)**
          - Added: RWL022 event handling for both integrations. ZHA `on_*`/`off_*` commands and Z2M `on_*`/`off_*` actions are normalized to the internal `power_*`/`hue_*` names, and Z2M `recall_0`/`recall_1` are treated as a Hue button short release.
          - Added: Brightness Control section with a mode selector per brightness button (Brightness Control or Normal Button), a shared Dimming Speed, and a Fallback Lights target.
          - Added: Brightness buttons dim the lights of whichever button the Last Pressed helper names. A short press applies one step; holding repeats a step every half second until release, capped at 60 steps.
          - Changed: buttons are now named for their physical function, so every input was renamed from `button_1`–`button_4` to `power`, `up`, `down` and `hue`.
          - Changed: the Last Pressed helper now stores a button name (`power`/`up`/`down`/`hue`) rather than a digit, so widen it to 5 characters. A button in Brightness Control mode no longer writes to the helper.
          - Removed: all dial rotation logic, along with the per-button Dimming Speed inputs it used. Dimming Speed is now a single setting in Brightness Control.
          - Removed: all media player support.

        - **2026.08.1: Fix dial brightness jumping while turning**
          - Fixed: spurious zero-step rotation messages were consuming the single-mode slot and issuing a brightness_step: 0 call, causing brightness to jump up and down while turning the dial. Added step_size > 0 guard alongside the existing step_size != 255 guard. Also fixes fast custom-action turns dropping clicks for the same reason.

        - **2026.07.1: Fix auto-adjust error when only one of brightness/color temp is enabled**
          - Fixed: "expected float for brightness_pct" error occurring when Auto-Adjust Brightness is off but Auto-Adjust Color Temperature is on (or vice versa). Replaced `omit` in typed numeric data fields with explicit `choose` branches per button: one call for both fields, one for brightness only, one for color temp only.

        - **2026.06.2: Fix adaptive auto-adjust only working for Button 1**
          - Fixed: Auto-Adjust now correctly applies to all buttons when multiple adaptive helpers update simultaneously (e.g. lights_bright + lights_dimmed schedulers firing at the same time). Previously, mode:single caused only the first trigger to execute, silently dropping the others. All buttons are now processed in a single automation run, eliminating the race condition.

        - **2026.06.1: Dial color temperature control and double press light mode**
          - Added: "Color Temperature" option in Rotate Mode, allowing the dial to adjust color temp instead of (or alongside) brightness
          - Added: Color Temp Speed input per button (1–10 slider), mirroring Dimming Speed to control how fast color temperature changes
          - Added: Rotate Mode Helper input per button (optional input_text entity that overrides the static Rotate Mode at runtime, enabling toggling between brightness and color temp)
          - Added: "Toggle Rotate Mode" action option in short release, long release, and double press light mode selectors
          - Added: Double Press Mode light selector per button (turn_on/turn_off/toggle/toggle_rotate_mode; double press previously had no built-in light mode)
          - Added: Separate "Auto-Adjust Brightness" and "Auto-Adjust Color Temperature" toggles per button, allowing dial color temperature control to coexist with adaptive/schedule brightness auto-adjust
          - Added: Button Helpers Configuration setup guide, explaining how to create the required Last Pressed helper and optional Rotate Mode helper, with a YAML example for `buttons.yaml`
          - Improved: "Dim" option in Rotate Mode renamed to "Brightness" (value `dim` → `brightness`; stored `dim` values are silently ignored, re-save automation to restore rotation if needed)
          - Breaking: "Auto-Adjust on Value Change" replaced by separate `_brightness` and `_color_temp` toggles, re-enable the relevant toggle(s) if previously active

        - **2026.04.1: Fix template warning in Z2M double-press detection**
          - Fixed: Added `| default('')` to `value_json.action` in the two `wait_for_trigger` blocks used for double-press detection
          - Fixed: Silences template variable warning triggered by spurious Z2M MQTT messages (linkquality, battery updates) that don't carry an action field

        - **2026.02.1: Label support, separate brightness/color reset, dial direction fix, Z2M integration tags**
          - Added: Label targets now work in Light Mode (uses label_entities() to resolve entities)
          - Added: Separate "Reset Brightness" and "Reset Color Temperature" toggles per button (replaces combined "Reset to Defaults")
          - Added: Z2M/ZHA integration tags on all custom action inputs so users know which actions are supported per integration
          - Fixed: Dial rotation direction confusion by switching from parallel to single automation mode
          - Improved: Z2M double tap detection updated to work with single automation mode (consume wait absorbs the second release)
          - Breaking: `button_X_short_release_reset` and `button_X_long_release_reset` replaced by `_brightness` and `_color` variants; reconfigure if you previously set these to false

        - **2026.01.3: Fix NoneType division errors in volume control and documentation improvements**
          - Fixed: Added `| int(0)` filter to all 8 volume_level templates for dial rotation
          - Fixed: Prevents "TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for /: 'NoneType' and 'int'" errors
          - Improved: Matches protective pattern already used in brightness templates
          - Improved: Added badges and reorganized documentation with better structure
          - Improved: Moved Version History and Schedule Helper Configuration to collapsed input sections

        - **2026.01.2: Fix NoneType multiplication and division errors in templates**
          - Fixed: "TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for *: 'NoneType' and 'int'" errors during dial rotation by adding int(0) default to step_size in brightness calculations
          - Fixed: "TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for /: 'NoneType' and 'int'" errors in media volume calculations by adding default(35) to button_X_volume
          - Improved: All brightness_step calculations now use: (step_size | int(0) * button_X_step_size / 10)
          - Improved: All current_volume calculations now use: (button_X_volume | default(35)) / 100
          - Note: These errors occurred in automations created before input defaults were added, or when trigger data doesn't include expected parameters

        - **2026.01.1: Fix Z2M MQTT subscription error for ZHA-only users**
          - Fixed: Z2M MQTT subscription errors when using ZHA-only configuration
          - Improved: Conditional MQTT trigger based on integration selection

        - **2025.12.2: Add adaptive lighting support to Philips Hue Tap Dial blueprint**
          - Added: Adaptive lighting mode with schedule helper and sensor integration
          - Added: Auto-adjust feature for automatic light updates on schedule changes
          - Enhanced: Support for brightness and color temperature from schedules and sensors

        - **2025.12.1: Major update - Z2M support, Auto-Adjust, Reset to Defaults, Dimming Speed**
          - Added: Zigbee2MQTT (Z2M) integration support alongside ZHA
          - Added: Auto-adjust lights when schedule changes
          - Added: Reset to defaults button action
          - Added: Configurable dimming speed per button
          - Improved: Documentation and organization

        - **2025.04.0: Change variables to be unique per button**
          - Changed: Made all variables unique per button for better isolation

        - **2025.02.0: Big v2 update with a lot of changes**
          - Major: Complete rewrite with many new features and improvements

        - **2025.01.1: Lights mode without schedules, cleanup of old syntax**
          - Added: Lights mode without requiring schedules
          - Improved: Code cleanup and syntax updates

        - **2025.01.0: Initial Version**
          - First release with basic Philips Hue Tap Dial Switch support
      icon: mdi:history
      collapsed: true
      input: {}
    button_helpers_info:
      name: Button Helpers Configuration
      description: |-
        One `input_text` helper is used by this blueprint.

        ### Setting up Packages (Optional)
        Organize helpers into packages for easier management. Create a `packages` folder in `/config/` and add to your configuration:

        ```yaml
        homeassistant:
          packages: !include_dir_named packages
        ```

        ### Last Pressed Helper (Required)
        Stores the name of the button that was last pressed: `power`, `up`, `down` or `hue`.
        When a brightness button is held or pressed, it dims the lights belonging to the button
        named here. **Each switch requires its own unique helper.**

        A button in Brightness Control mode never writes to this helper, so dimming does not
        steal the target away from the button whose lights you are adjusting. That means the
        helper normally alternates between `power` and `hue`.

        Until a button has been pressed the helper is empty, and dimming falls back to the
        Fallback Lights target, or to the Power button's lights if that is also empty.

        ### YAML Example
        Create `/config/packages/buttons.yaml`:

        ```yaml
        input_text:
          living_room_button_last_pressed:
            name: "Living Room Button Last Pressed"
            icon: mdi:gesture-tap-button
            min: 0
            max: 5
            mode: text
            pattern: "power|up|down|hue"
        ```
      icon: mdi:gesture-tap-button
      collapsed: true
      input: {}
    schedule_helper_info:
      name: Schedule Helper Configuration
      description: |-
        Create time-based brightness and color adjustments using Home Assistant schedule helpers.

        ### Setting up Packages (Optional)
        Organize schedules into packages for easier management. Create a `packages` folder in `/config/` and add to your configuration:

        ```yaml
        homeassistant:
          packages: !include_dir_named packages
        ```

        ### Schedule YAML Example
        Create `/config/packages/lights.yaml` with your schedules:

        ```yaml
        schedule:
          lights_bright:
            name: "Lights Bright"
            icon: mdi:lightbulb-auto
            monday:
              - from: "00:00:00"
                to: "09:00:00"
                data:
                  brightness_pct: 30
                  color_temp_kelvin: 3333
              - from: "09:00:00"
                to: "23:00:00"
                data:
                  brightness_pct: 90
                  color_temp_kelvin: 3333
              - from: "23:00:00"
                to: "24:00:00"
                data:
                  brightness_pct: 30
                  color_temp_kelvin: 3333
            # Repeat pattern for tuesday through sunday
        ```

        You can create multiple schedules with different brightness levels (e.g., `lights_bright` and `lights_dimmed`) for different scenarios.

        ### Schedule Flexibility

        **Optional Fields:** If a schedule lacks certain data fields (like `transition`), the blueprint reverts to default values configured in the automation. This allows selective override of specific parameters while maintaining other preset defaults.

        **Supported Schedule Attributes:**
        - `brightness_pct`: Brightness percentage (0-100)
        - `color_temp_kelvin`: Color temperature in Kelvin
        - `transition`: Optional transition time in seconds

        ### Auto-Adjust Feature

        When enabled, the blueprint automatically updates lights when the schedule changes (e.g., when moving from morning to afternoon time block):
        - Only affects lights that are currently ON
        - Configurable transition duration (default: 5 minutes)
        - Applies current schedule's brightness and color temperature
        - Can be enabled/disabled per button
      icon: mdi:calendar-clock
      collapsed: true
      input: {}
    integration_type:
      name: Integration Type
      description: |-
        `required`

        Select which integration(s) to use for the Philips Hue Dimmer Switch. You can select Z2M, ZHA, or both.
      default: []
      selector:
        select:
          options:
            - label: Zigbee2MQTT (Z2M)
              value: z2m
            - label: Zigbee Home Automation (ZHA)
              value: zha
          multiple: true
    z2m:
      name: Zigbee2MQTT (Z2M)
      description: Configure Zigbee2MQTT integration settings.
      icon: mdi:zigbee
      collapsed: true
      input:
        z2m_base_topic:
          name: Base Topic
          description: |-
            `optional` `text`

            MQTT base topic for Zigbee2MQTT installation (usually `zigbee2mqtt`). Leave empty if not using Z2M.
          default: ""
          selector:
            text: {}
        z2m_device_name:
          name: Device Friendly Name
          description: |-
            `optional` `text`

            Friendly name of your Philips Hue Dimmer Switch in Z2M (case-sensitive, as shown in Z2M UI). Leave empty if not using Z2M.
          default: ""
          selector:
            text: {}
    zha:
      name: Zigbee Home Automation (ZHA)
      description: Configure ZHA integration settings.
      icon: mdi:zigbee
      collapsed: true
      input:
        zha_remote:
          name: Remote Device (ZHA)
          description: |-
            `optional` `device`

            Select the Philips Hue Dimmer Switch device from ZHA. Leave empty if not using ZHA.
          default: {}
          selector:
            device:
              entity:
                - domain:
                    - sensor
                  device_class:
                    - battery
              filter:
                - integration: zha
                  manufacturer: Signify Netherlands B.V.
                  model: RWL022
              multiple: false
    last_pressed:
      name: Last Pressed Input Text Helper
      description: |-
        `required` `entity`

        Create an input text helper within Home Assistant to keep track
        of the last button pressed. It stores `power`, `up`, `down` or `hue`, and the
        brightness buttons use it to decide which lights to dim.
        **Each switch requires a unique helper!**
      selector:
        entity:
          filter:
            - domain:
                - input_text
          multiple: false
    brightness_control:
      name: Brightness Control
      description: Configure what the Brightness Up and Brightness Down buttons do.
      icon: mdi:brightness-6
      collapsed: true
      input:
        up_button_mode:
          name: Brightness Up Button Mode
          description: |-
            `optional` `select`

            **Brightness Control**: the button dims the lights of whichever button was last
            pressed, tracked by the Last Pressed helper. Its own Light Mode actions are ignored.

            **Normal Button**: the button behaves like the Power and Hue buttons, running its
            own Light Mode actions and becoming the new Last Pressed target.
          default: brightness
          selector:
            select:
              options:
                - label: Brightness Control
                  value: brightness
                - label: Normal Button
                  value: normal
              custom_value: false
              multiple: false
        down_button_mode:
          name: Brightness Down Button Mode
          description: |-
            `optional` `select`

            **Brightness Control**: the button dims the lights of whichever button was last
            pressed, tracked by the Last Pressed helper. Its own Light Mode actions are ignored.

            **Normal Button**: the button behaves like the Power and Hue buttons, running its
            own Light Mode actions and becoming the new Last Pressed target.
          default: brightness
          selector:
            select:
              options:
                - label: Brightness Control
                  value: brightness
                - label: Normal Button
                  value: normal
              custom_value: false
              multiple: false
        brightness_speed:
          name: Dimming Speed
          description: |-
            `optional` `number`

            How much brightness changes per step (1=slowest/smoothest, 10=fastest/jumpiest).
            A short press applies one step; holding repeats a step every half second.
            At the default of 5, holding sweeps the full range in about five seconds.
          default: 5
          selector:
            number:
              min: 1
              max: 10
              step: 1
              mode: slider
        brightness_fallback_light:
          name: Fallback Lights
          description: |-
            `optional` `target`

            Lights to dim when the Last Pressed helper is empty or holds an unexpected value,
            which is the case until a button has been pressed. Leave empty to fall back to the
            Power button's lights instead.
          default: []
          selector:
            target:
              entity:
                - domain:
                    - light
    power_custom:
      name: Power Button - Custom Actions
      icon: mdi:power
      collapsed: true
      input:
        power_press:
          name: Short Press
          description: |-
            `optional` `action` `ZHA`

            Action to run on a short press of the Power button.
          default: []
          selector:
            action: {}
        power_short_release:
          name: Short Release
          description: |-
            `optional` `action` `Z2M` `ZHA`

            Action to run on a release of the Power button after a short press.
          default: []
          selector:
            action: {}
        power_hold:
          name: Long Press
          description: |-
            `optional` `action` `Z2M` `ZHA`

            Action to run on a long press of the Power button. Will repeat while the button is held.
          default: []
          selector:
            action: {}
        power_long_release:
          name: Long Release
          description: |-
            `optional` `action` `Z2M` `ZHA`

            Action to run when the Power button is released after a long press.
          default: []
          selector:
            action: {}
        power_double:
          name: Double Press
          description: |-
            `optional` `action` `Z2M` `ZHA`

            Action to run on a double press of the Power button.
          default: []
          selector:
            action: {}
    power_light:
      name: Power Button - Light Mode
      icon: mdi:lightbulb
      collapsed: true
      input:
        power_light:
          name: Lights
          description: |-
            `optional` `target`

            The lights to control with this button.
          default: []
          selector:
            target:
              entity:
                - domain:
                    - light
        power_short_release_light_mode:
          name: Short Release Mode
          description: |-
            `optional` `select`

            Light actions for short release. Multiple selections trigger simultaneously.
          default: turn_on
          selector:
            select:
              options:
                - label: Turn On
                  value: turn_on
                - label: Turn Off
                  value: turn_off
                - label: Toggle
                  value: toggle
              custom_value: false
              multiple: true
        power_long_release_light_mode:
          name: Long Release Mode
          description: |-
            `optional` `select`

            Light actions for long release. Multiple selections trigger simultaneously.
          default: turn_off
          selector:
            select:
              options:
                - label: Turn On
                  value: turn_on
                - label: Turn Off
                  value: turn_off
                - label: Toggle
                  value: toggle
              custom_value: false
              multiple: true
        power_double_light_mode:
          name: Double Press Mode
          description: |-
            `optional` `select`

            Light actions for double press. Multiple selections trigger simultaneously.
          default: []
          selector:
            select:
              options:
                - label: Turn On
                  value: turn_on
                - label: Turn Off
                  value: turn_off
                - label: Toggle
                  value: toggle
              custom_value: false
              multiple: true
    power_light_settings:
      name: Power Button - Light Mode Settings
      icon: mdi:cog
      collapsed: true
      input:
        power_light_adjustment_mode:
          name: Light Adjustment Mode
          description: |-
            `optional` `select`

            Choose where brightness and color temperature values come from:
            - **Static**: Use the default values configured below
            - **Adaptive**: Use input_number helpers updated by the Adaptive Lighting Scheduler blueprint
            - **Schedule**: Use a schedule entity for time-based adjustments
          default: static
          selector:
            select:
              options:
                - label: Static
                  value: static
                - label: Adaptive
                  value: adaptive
                - label: Schedule
                  value: schedule
              multiple: false
        power_light_brightness:
          name: Default Brightness
          description: |-
            `optional` `number`

            Default brightness percentage (fallback when adaptive/schedule is not set or lacks this attribute).
          default: 100
          selector:
            number:
              min: 0
              max: 100
              step: 5
              unit_of_measurement: "%"
              mode: slider
        power_light_color:
          name: Default Color Temperature
          description: |-
            `optional` `color_temp`

            Default color temperature in Kelvin (fallback when adaptive/schedule is not set or lacks this attribute).
          default: 3333
          selector:
            color_temp:
              unit: kelvin
              min: 2000
        power_light_transition:
          name: Default Transition
          description: |-
            `optional` `number`

            Default transition duration in seconds (fallback when schedule is not set or lacks this attribute).
          default: 1
          selector:
            number:
              min: 0
              max: 10
              step: 1
              mode: slider
        power_light_adaptive_brightness:
          name: Adaptive Brightness Helper
          description: |-
            `optional` `entity`

            Input number helper containing adaptive brightness (0-100). Only used when Light Adjustment Mode is "Adaptive".
          default: []
          selector:
            entity:
              filter:
                - domain:
                    - input_number
              multiple: false
        power_light_adaptive_color_temp:
          name: Adaptive Color Temperature Helper
          description: |-
            `optional` `entity`

            Input number helper containing adaptive color temperature in Kelvin. Only used when Light Adjustment Mode is "Adaptive".
          default: []
          selector:
            entity:
              filter:
                - domain:
                    - input_number
              multiple: false
        power_light_schedule:
          name: Schedule Helper
          description: |-
            `optional` `entity`

            Schedule helper for time-based brightness and color adjustments. Only used when Light Adjustment Mode is "Schedule". **Schedules can be reused between lights.**
          default: []
          selector:
            entity:
              filter:
                - domain:
                    - schedule
              multiple: false
        power_light_auto_adjust_brightness:
          name: Auto-Adjust Brightness on Value Change
          description: |-
            `optional` `boolean`

            Automatically update light brightness when adaptive or schedule values change. Only affects currently on lights.
          default: false
          selector:
            boolean: {}
        power_light_auto_adjust_color_temp:
          name: Auto-Adjust Color Temperature on Value Change
          description: |-
            `optional` `boolean`

            Automatically update light color temperature when adaptive or schedule values change. Only affects currently on lights.
          default: false
          selector:
            boolean: {}
        power_light_auto_adjust_transition:
          name: Auto-Adjust Transition
          description: |-
            `optional` `number`

            Transition duration in seconds when auto-adjusting lights.
          default: 300
          selector:
            number:
              min: 0
              max: 600
              step: 30
              unit_of_measurement: s
              mode: slider
        power_short_release_reset_brightness:
          name: Reset Brightness on Short Release
          description: |-
            `optional` `boolean`

            Apply the default brightness value when turning on. Disable to maintain current brightness.
          default: true
          selector:
            boolean: {}
        power_short_release_reset_color:
          name: Reset Color Temperature on Short Release
          description: |-
            `optional` `boolean`

            Apply the default color temperature when turning on. Disable to maintain current color temperature.
          default: true
          selector:
            boolean: {}
        power_long_release_reset_brightness:
          name: Reset Brightness on Long Release
          description: |-
            `optional` `boolean`

            Apply the default brightness value on long release. Disable to maintain current brightness.
          default: true
          selector:
            boolean: {}
        power_long_release_reset_color:
          name: Reset Color Temperature on Long Release
          description: |-
            `optional` `boolean`

            Apply the default color temperature on long release. Disable to maintain current color temperature.
          default: true
          selector:
            boolean: {}
    up_custom:
      name: Brightness Up Button - Custom Actions
      icon: mdi:arrow-up-bold
      collapsed: true
      input:
        up_press:
          name: Short Press
          description: |-
            `optional` `action` `ZHA`

            Action to run on a short press of the Brightness Up button.
          default: []
          selector:
            action: {}
        up_short_release:
          name: Short Release
          description: |-
            `optional` `action` `Z2M` `ZHA`

            Action to run on a release of the Brightness Up button after a short press.
          default: []
          selector:
            action: {}
        up_hold:
          name: Long Press
          description: |-
            `optional` `action` `Z2M` `ZHA`

            Action to run on a long press of the Brightness Up button. Will repeat while the button is held.
          default: []
          selector:
            action: {}
        up_long_release:
          name: Long Release
          description: |-
            `optional` `action` `Z2M` `ZHA`

            Action to run when the Brightness Up button is released after a long press.
          default: []
          selector:
            action: {}
        up_double:
          name: Double Press
          description: |-
            `optional` `action` `Z2M` `ZHA`

            Action to run on a double press of the Brightness Up button.
          default: []
          selector:
            action: {}
    up_light:
      name: Brightness Up Button - Light Mode
      icon: mdi:lightbulb
      collapsed: true
      input:
        up_light:
          name: Lights
          description: |-
            `optional` `target`

            The lights to control with this button.
          default: []
          selector:
            target:
              entity:
                - domain:
                    - light
        up_short_release_light_mode:
          name: Short Release Mode
          description: |-
            `optional` `select`

            Light actions for short release. Multiple selections trigger simultaneously.
          default: turn_on
          selector:
            select:
              options:
                - label: Turn On
                  value: turn_on
                - label: Turn Off
                  value: turn_off
                - label: Toggle
                  value: toggle
              custom_value: false
              multiple: true
        up_long_release_light_mode:
          name: Long Release Mode
          description: |-
            `optional` `select`

            Light actions for long release. Multiple selections trigger simultaneously.
          default: turn_off
          selector:
            select:
              options:
                - label: Turn On
                  value: turn_on
                - label: Turn Off
                  value: turn_off
                - label: Toggle
                  value: toggle
              custom_value: false
              multiple: true
        up_double_light_mode:
          name: Double Press Mode
          description: |-
            `optional` `select`

            Light actions for double press. Multiple selections trigger simultaneously.
          default: []
          selector:
            select:
              options:
                - label: Turn On
                  value: turn_on
                - label: Turn Off
                  value: turn_off
                - label: Toggle
                  value: toggle
              custom_value: false
              multiple: true
    up_light_settings:
      name: Brightness Up Button - Light Mode Settings
      icon: mdi:cog
      collapsed: true
      input:
        up_light_adjustment_mode:
          name: Light Adjustment Mode
          description: |-
            `optional` `select`

            Choose where brightness and color temperature values come from:
            - **Static**: Use the default values configured below
            - **Adaptive**: Use input_number helpers updated by the Adaptive Lighting Scheduler blueprint
            - **Schedule**: Use a schedule entity for time-based adjustments
          default: static
          selector:
            select:
              options:
                - label: Static
                  value: static
                - label: Adaptive
                  value: adaptive
                - label: Schedule
                  value: schedule
              multiple: false
        up_light_brightness:
          name: Default Brightness
          description: |-
            `optional` `number`

            Default brightness percentage (fallback when adaptive/schedule is not set or lacks this attribute).
          default: 100
          selector:
            number:
              min: 0
              max: 100
              step: 5
              unit_of_measurement: "%"
              mode: slider
        up_light_color:
